  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The researchers developed a multiagent reinforcement learning algorithm, STIA-MARL, for multi-intersection traffic signal control that incorporates historical traffic flows to capture dynamic spatiotemporal correlations. The model uses a custom graph structure to modify adjacency relationships, which improves how a shared policy network adapts to different intersections. Testing on synthetic and real-world datasets showed at least an 11.5% reduction in average travel time compared to existing state-of-the-art methods.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that incorporating historical flow data directly into the spatial modeling of traffic networks, rather than relying on static spatial relationships, significantly improves the efficiency of coordinated traffic signal control."
    }
